    "title_en": "Updated T2K measurement of neutrino oscillation parameters with the first data from the Gadolinium-loaded far detector",
    "abstract_en": "The T2K experiment presents updated measurements of neutrino oscillation parameters using $21.4(16.3)\\times10^{20}$ protons on target (POT) in (anti-)neutrino mode at the far detector, Super-Kamiokande. This analysis uses an additional neutrino dataset of $1.7 \\times 10^{20}$ POT compared to the previous result, and for the very first time, data collected with Super-Kamiokande doped with Gadolinium (Gd). Significant improvements were introduced in the far detector selection and systematic error treatment. Both semi-frequentist and Bayesian analyses are presented, including results on $\\sin^{2} θ_{23}$, $Δm^2_{32} $, $\\sin^{2} θ_{13}$ and $δ_{CP}$. Both analyses favor normal mass ordering with a nearly maximal CP-violating phase and are compatible with neutrino maximal mixing, slightly favouring the upper $θ_{23}$ octant.",
